{
  "dom_id": "step-q11757",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-6,-4).$",
  "worked_solution": "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-6,-4),$ we can substitute $x=-6$ and $y=-4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\ 16 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{2}{3})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{8}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
